// wadinfo.momo - what is in a WAD, and what is wrong with it (DESIGN §41).
//
//   wadinfo DOOM.WAD
//   wadinfo BASE.WAD PATCH.WAD
//   wadinfo /s BASE.WAD PATCH.WAD     overrides and damage in full, the rest counted
//   wadinfo /l DOOM.WAD               the listing alone, and nothing checked
//
// The program is `shared/lib/moinfo.momo`, which says what it prints and why. It
// is a library so that each mode can be a project of its own, since a project
// has one command tail.
//
// The fixture is `BASE.WAD` and `PATCH.WAD`, built by the host writer from the
// manifests in `fixture/` - the command for each is at the top of its manifest.
// PATCH.WAD carries something for every finding. This project runs them with no
// switch; `wadsum` and `wadlist` run copies of them under `/s` and `/l`.

include "lib/moinfo.momo"

infoRun()
